John Mulaney returned home to Studio 8H for his seventh time hosting Saturday Night Live .

In his opening monologue, the 4x Emmy winner and former SNL writer recalled his time working on the NBC sketch comedy show from 2008 to 2013.

&#8220;One of the only difficult things about working here was dealing with hosts,&#8221; said Mulaney. &#8220;So, it's fun when I host, because it's like there's no host.&#8221;

During his quick stand-up set, Mulaney noted how everything made sense after finding out his boomer dad was on the autism spectrum. &#8220;He doesn't know he's autistic. He'll find out right at this airs,&#8221; he quipped. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The comedian also called out Boomers' hypocritical complaints about Gen Z and joked about about his son's toddler friends, which transitioned into a roast of RFK Jr., complete with a brutal impression. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

&#8220;You dumbass, your thing can't be the measles,&#8221; said Mulaney, adding: &#8220;Yeah, I called him Bobby. I've known him for over a decade. You shouldn't be part of the government if I've known you for over a decade.&#8221;

In a news report sketch of a plane crash on a flight from Turkey to Newark, Mulaney played a survivor who attempted to play off his hair transplant bandages as injuries from the accident. Ben Marshall played another survivor with similar bandages, plus some very plump lip injections. &#8220;Unfortunately, some bees swarmed the plane, Sully style,&#8221; he claimed.

&#8220;I think those were geese,&#8221; noted Ashley Padilla's reporter character as Marcello Hernandez played a pilot who got penile enlargement surgery.

The sketch ended with Kam Patterson as NYC's former Mayor Eric Adams, who was also on the flight.

The next sketch was a fake pharmaceutical commercial for &#8220;Sister,&#8221; which is just Mulaney, Andrew Dismukes and Kenan Thompson relying on their sisters to take care of their sick parents. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In another sketch, Padilla played Kathy, the &#8220;worst person on earth&#8221; who crashes her co-workers' happy hour, where she's nursing a fishbowl. Mulaney tries to make his colleagues Day, Thompson and Sarah Sherman to ignore her, despite her hilariously awkward demeanor.

As Jeremy Culhane hosted the fake brewery show Gettin It Done , he had a few autumn IPAs with Mulaney's Brewmaster Kenny, which led to the pair drunkenly making out multiple times.

&#8220;Well, turns out it was the beer,&#8221; said Culhane's host Chris Gut after a steamy back-and-forth. &#8220;We hung out sober one day, and it was like, nothing.&#8221;

On &#8220;Weekend Update,&#8221; co-host Colin Jost commented on the FAA's historic grounding of planes on Friday. &#8220;Suddenly, ferry transportation is looking pretty reliable,&#8221; he quipped.

Meanwhile, co-host Michael Che showed off his own RFK Jr. impression. &#8220;Put me in the cast, Lorne!&#8221; he declared.

In &#8220;The Little Park of Horrors,&#8221; Mulaney played a horse-drawn carriage operator mourning NYC's recent ban, &#8220;and for no reason at all, except animal cruelty and human murders.&#8221; In the musical sketch, he introduces a series of characters, including Veronika Slowikowska as a woman still finishing the marathon, singing a parody of &#8220;Don't Rain on My Parade.&#8221; Tommy Brennan plays a pedicab driver coming for Mulaney's job with a take on &#8220;Anything You Can Do (I Can Do Better).&#8221;

Day played a homeless man ranting about God, while Thompson played a cloud of weed smoke, backed by Sherman, Grace Reiter and Saidah Belo-Osagie in a rendition of Cats &#8216; &#8220;Mr. Mistoffelees.&#8221; James Austin Johnson played &#8220;Park Slope Cuck&#8221; singing his parody of &#8220;Maria&#8221; from West Side Story , entitled &#8220;Mamdani.&#8221;

In another Bowen Yang appearance, following the cold open , the SNL alum served his current Broadway role from Oh Mary! with a parody of the Dreamgirls song &#8220;And I'm Telling You I'm Not Going&#8221; about the MTA.

The sketch included an expert callback to Padilla's Kathy character. &#8220;We talking transpo?&#8221; she asked with her fishbowl drink in hand.

In the final sketch, Day and several of the cast members played Boomers at Woodstock, planning to buy all the houses one day, keep all the money, scare their kids about weed and make college more expensive.

Marking Mulaney's seventh time hosting Saturday Night Live , following his time as sketch writer from 2008 to 2013, Phoebe Bridgers joined him this weekend in her second gig as musical guest.

Bowen Yang made a surprise appearance on Saturday Night Live to portray former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang to warn a group of tech billionaires about how to decipher between "a woman who would actually want to have sex with you and a woman who is clearly a spy."

John Mulaney , who served as the host of the episode, kicked off the cold open by welcoming the group of moguls, including Sam Altman (Ben Marshall), Peter Thiel (James Austin Johnson), Elon Musk (Jeremy Culhane), Mark Zuckerberg (Andrew Dismukes) and Dario Amodei (Jane Wickline). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories TV Shane Gillis Addresses 'SNL' Monologue Backlash, Says He Promised the Show There Would Be "No Controversy" TV TV Ratings: 'SNL' Hits Two-Year High With Druski as Host

"We are here to discuss an extremely sensitive matter of national security," Mulaney began.

"America needs you to learn the difference between a woman who would actually want to have sex with you and a woman who is clearly a spy,&#8221; he said. &#8220;Former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigned this week after he was caught having an affair with an alleged Chinese spy."

"What do you think the lesson is here?" he asked, to which Wickline's Amodei responded, "Never date a Chinese woman." Dismukes' Zuckerberg offered, "Never date a human woman."

"Never date anyone unless they become the Anti-Christ," Johnson's Thiel said. Mulaney joked that he needed to "chill with the Anti-Christ stuff," which prompted him to respond, "Show us some respect. We do a lot for this country. Name one time technology has let us down."

The comedian then pointed to current events: &#8220;Yesterday, when every plane in America was grounded.&#8221; Thiel asked for &#8220;one more&#8221; example, which Mulaney affirmed, &#8220;The day before that when Microsoft Outlook went dark!&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

He then showed the tech billionaires a few venn diagrams to try and spell things out for the men, making way for Yang's surprise return. &#8220;You know what, maybe what would help is if I hand it over to someone who learned this lesson the hard way,&#8221; Mulaney said, as the former SNL star then entered the scene.

&#8220;It's me! Jensen &#8216;hide your wife' Huang!&#8221; Yang said. &#8220;When you invite Jensen over, you know it's about to go down.&#8221;

He joked, &#8220;Fellas, don't be like me. Remember, women don't like guys like us. That's how we became guys like us.&#8221;

Yang exited the SNL cast last December, with Saturday's cameo marking his first appearance on the show since he left. He departed the series mid-season 51 with a heartfelt farewell sketch alongside Ariana Grande.

Later in the Dec. 14 episode, Yang also appeared in a sketch as Mary Todd Lincoln, the role he began performing on Broadway this September in Oh, Mary! He sang a spoof of &#8220;And I Am Telling You I'm Not Going,&#8221; which prompted Mulaney to joke, &#8220;Wow! Now that'll turn Abraham straight again.&#8221;

It was also announced in the episode that Amanda Seyfried will host the Dec. 5 episode of SNL , with Don Toliver as musical guest.

During Mulaney's monologue, he did a light Robert F. Kennedy Jr. impression, which merely turned out to be more of a criticism of the United States Secretary of Health and Human Services.

He started by explaining that as a father, he often is around a lot of toddlers. &#8220;Whenever I'm with my son's 4-year-old, 5-year-old friends, whenever I'm with a group of toddlers at art camp, preschool play dates, there's always at least one little kid who for some reason, has a very scratchy or hoarse voice.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;Whenever a few are at my house, there's always one like, &#8216;Do you have water balloons?' Like, &#8216;Do you live alone?'&#8221; Mulaney said, continuing to repeat questions that his children's friends ask him, using a raspy voice while saying, &#8220;I'm the U.S. Secretary of Health and Human Services. My father was a good man, and I'm a lousy man, but I have same name. Am I good if I have same name as father?&#8221;

Mulaney continued his impression, &#8220;No, please, let me be in charge of your bone and your tummy. Please allow me to control how your blood feels in your butt and everywhere. Stop the science! Robitussin taken during menstruation will cause telekinesis. This is clear from the pamphlets in my rental car.'"

He then returned to his own voice, continuing to criticize RFK Jr. &#8220;I have right-wing friends that used to be down with him, no one likes him. You dumbass: Your thing can't be the measles.&#8221;

Mulaney previously served as an SNL writer from 2008-2012. Although he was never a castmember, he has since returned to the show multiple times since his departure, making a plethora of cameos and hosting seven times.

The comedian was joined by Phoebe Bridgers as musical guest, marking her second solo appearance (she's also been on SNL as part of the musical group Boygenius).

So far on season 52 , Jalen Brunson , Dakota Johnson , Shane Gillis , Inde Navarrette and Druski have each hosted.

Bowen Yang returned to Saturday Night Live to play Jensen Huang in the show's cold open, a skewering of tech billionaires susceptibility to honey pots, or being wooed by attractive women and thinking that they genuinely are in it for the romance.

The skit follows Huang's resignation as CEO of Nvidia following revelations that he had an affair with a woman who may have been a Chinese spy, and another affair with a subordinate. That sent shares of the company tumbling.

&#8220;When you invite Jensen over, you know what is about to go down &#8212; the S&P 500,&#8221; Yang's Huang said. &#8220;That's right &#8212; I'm into BDSM &#8212; Breaking Da Stock Market.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The premise of the skit had John Mulaney, this week's host, playing a CIA official trying to instruct the gathered tech billionaires to be on the lookout for women who show interest in them.

&#8220;America needs you to learn the difference between a woman who would actually want to have sex with you and a woman who is clearly a spy,&#8221; the CIA official told them. &#8220;Now you all saw former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resined this week after he was acught having an affair with an alleged Chinese spy. What do you think the lesson is here?&#8221;

&#8220;Yeah, never date a Chinese woman,&#8221; Anthropic's Dario Amodei (Jane Wickline) answered.

&#8220;No,&#8221; the CIA official said.

&#8220;Never date a human,&#8221; said Mark Zuckerberg (Andrew Dismukes).

&#8220;No,&#8221; the CIA official said.

&#8220;Never date anyone lest they become the Antichrist,&#8221; responded Peter Thiel (James Austin Johnson).

&#8220;No, and Peter, you got to chill with the Antichrist stuff,&#8221; the CIA official told him.

The recent midterms in many ways were a backlash against the AI overlords, with opposition to data centers reflecting fears of AI's impact on jobs and humanity.

&#8220;Show us some respect. We do a lot for this country,&#8221; Thiel told the CIA official. &#8220;Name one time technology has let us down.&#8221;

&#8220;Yesterday, when every plane in America was grounded,&#8221; the CIA official answered. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;Okay, name one more time.&#8221;

&#8220;The day before that, when Microsoft went dark,&#8221; the CIA official reminded.

Mulaney's character went on, &#8220;Look, I get it, I can't imagine how disorienting this has been for you to go from these bug-eyed little weirdos to being gods. I mean, never in the history of our species have people as pale and strange as you, a) survived, and b) been given all the world's wealth and power.&#8221;

The skit also featured Ben Marhsall as OpenAI's Sam Altman and Jeremy Culhane's return as an Elon Musk, incomprehensible to the point where the CIA official has to spray him with a water bottle to shut him up.

The CIA official tried to get across the dangers they were facing in getting hooked in to a spy plot.

