The tour offers an opportunity to witness problem-solving in real time. For Carlile and the twins, perhaps the biggest problem was obliging a request for Alanis Morissette's &#8220;Uninvited.&#8221; This was not because of recent unfamiliarity with the tune &#x2014; they performed it nearly every night on this year's &#8220;Human&#8221; arena tour, among the encores &#x2014; but because they'd never done it as an acoustic trio. Without the heightened drama of a string section and the number's signature piano notes. &#8220;I have no idea how we're gonna do this without strings. Love will find a way,&#8221; Carlile said. &#8220;And no piano? That's the whole song!&#8221; But she and the brothers found their path to make it a pure guitar-and-bass rock &#8216;n' roll scorcher, followed by an exultant &#8220;We don't need no stinking strings!&#8221; (With implicit apologies, undoubtedly, to SistaStrings.)

