Saying this was the best show I've ever seen by Carlile and company probably without saying, after saying all of that; at times, I got to thinking it was one of the best shows I've ever seen from anyone, out of untold thousands. Concert hyperbole is a dangerous thing, but I found myself hard-pressed to recall comparable instances in which I'd seen rock &#8216;n' roll performers so throughly committed to the moment, not just for a moment but for close to three hours of them. Maybe that's because I have a worse memory than Carlile and the Hanseroths, but more likely because this really is as good as it gets, if you have a taste for the rare intersection where hair-trigger meets tear-jerk. Adjust your settings for how many hundreds of dollars you'd pay for a resale ticket for the remaining dates accordingly.

